  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "State vs . Dilip on 29 March, 2023 In The Court Of Ms. Anamika: Mm-06, Ndd, Phc, New Delhi State Vs. Dilip Fir No.: 93/2011 P.S.: Tuglak Road U/Sec.: 279/338 Ipc & 3/181, 39/192 and 146/196 Mv Act Judgment :",
    "facts": "In the present case, accused Dilip is facing trial for offences punishable under Section 279/338 IPC & 3/181, 146/196/39/192 MV Act on the allegations that on 24.11.2011 at about 1.00 am in front of H. NO. 20 A, P.R. Road, within the jurisdiction of PS Tughlak Road falling within the jurisdiction of PS Tughlak Road, accused was driving a car (Maruti Van bearing No. DL11LE-6376) rashly and negligently and while driving so, accused hit a vehicle on the rear side of DTC Bus bearing NO. FIR No. 93/2011 PS Tuglak Road State vs. Dilip Page No. 1 of 9 DL-1PC-8565 resulting a grievous injuries to his co-passenger Ram Snehi. 2. After completion of investigation, charge sheet was filed on 08.02.2013 and cognizance was taken on same day. Copy of charge sheet was also supplied to accused on the said date and notice for offences punishable U/s. 279/304A IPC was given to accused on 26.08.2013, to which he pleaded not guilty and claimed trial. 3. To prove its case, prosecution has examined seven witnesses. 4. PW1 Sh. Ram Snehi has deposed that he was coming after purchasing vegetables and other food material on the van and the van was driven by the accused. The offending vehicle was driven by the accused in a high speed and in rash and negligent manner. Due to high speed the vehicle which was driven by the accused collided with the bus standing at bus stand due to which the complainant and the accused got injured. After that they have been taken to the hospital by the police officials. PW1 has identified the accused. State vs . Dilip on 29 March, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/71614847/ 1 5. PW2 Sh. Ram Charan who has deposed that in the year 2011, he conducted mechanical inspection of a bus bearing registration no. DL 1PC 8565 at PS tughlak Road, Delhi and also prepared a report which is now Ex. PW-2/A. FIR No. 93/2011 PS Tuglak Road State vs. Dilip Page No. 2 of 9 6. PW3 Sh. Anand Singh, who has deposed that on 24.11.2011, he was posted a a conductor in DTC bus bearing registration no. DL 1PC 8565. he deposed that when the bus was halted at a bus stop in its box for boarding and de-boarding of the passengers, suddenly he heard a very load noise which came from the back side of the bus. When he went to back side of the bus he saw that one van bearing registration no. DL 1LE 6376 of white colour was struck on the backside of the bus and its driver and passengers also got struck inside the van due to the impact. Both the rescued from the van and were taken to the hospital with the help of public persons and both were taken to the hospital by PCR van. The witness has failed to identify the accused as driver of the said van, rather he stated that the accused was sitting on the passenger side of the van. 7. PW4 is Sh. Parmod Kumar, who has deposed that on 24.11.2011, he was posted as a driver in a DTC bus bearing registration no. DL 1PC 8565. He deposed that when the bus was halted at a bus stop in its box for boarding and de-boarding of the passengers, sunndely he heard a very load noise which came from the back side of the bus. Both the rescued from the van and were taken to the hospital with the help of public persons and both were taken to the FIR No. 93/2011 PS Tuglak Road State vs. Dilip Page No. 3 of 9 hospital by PCR van. The witness has correctly identified the accused as a driver of the said van. The bus was seized by the IO vide seizure memo Ex. PW1/B. 8. PW5 is Ct. Anish who joined the investigation with IO/SI Gourav Gupta and accused namely Dilip Kumar was arrested from Gali no. 15, Khajoori Khas. After interrogation, the accused was arrested by him vide arrest memo already Ex. PW-4/C. 9. PW 6 is Sh. Arvinder Singh (Mechanical expert) who has deposed that he went to PS Tuglak Road, where he met SI Gaurav Gupta. The Maruti Van bearing No. DL 1LE 6376 which was shown by SI Gaurav Gupta. 10. PW 7 ASI Mahbir, has deposed that he was posted as Constable at PS Tuglak Road. He alongwith IO SI Gaurav Gupta went to the spot. They found one DTC bus bearing no. DL 1PC 8565 and one Maruti Van bearing no. DL 1 LE 6376 in accidental condition. The injured/driver of Maruti Van and the other injured who was sitting next to the driver of the Maruti Van were already taken to RML hospital. IO interrogated teh driver of the bus namely Parmod Kumar and conductor Anand Singh who were present at the spot. IO left him at hte spot and went to RML hospital. After some time, IO came back at the spot and handed over Tehrir to him. After that he went to the police station for the registration of FIR and original rukka and the same handed over to the IO. The driver of the offending vehicle identified by him. FIR No. 93/2011 PS Tuglak Road State vs. Dilip Page No. 4 of 9 The photographs of both the vehicles shown to the witness and the same were identified by him and same is Ex. A7. 11. Vide separate statement under Section 294 Cr.P.C., accused admitted copy of FIR no. 93/2011 PS Tuglak Road, DD no. 7A dated 24.11.2011, MLC no. 196411/2011 prepared by Dr. Anand Vishal, CMO, Dr. RML Hospital, opinion on MLC 196411/2011 prepared by Dr. Manish Rawat, R. Dr. RML Hospital, MLC no. 196406/2011 prepared by Dr. Ravinder Singh, CMO, Dr. RML Hospital, Superdarinama of DTC Bus bearing registration number DL 1PC 8565, photographs of the spot taken by the Ct. Sandeep and consequential witnesses were dropped from examination. Thereafter, PE was closed. 12. Statement of accused was recorded U/Sec. 313 Cr.P.C. r/w Section 281 Cr.P.C. on 06.02.2023 wherein he denied the case of the prosecution and pleaded innocence. Accused stated that he does not want to lead defence evidence.",
